{"absent":["Virtqueue layout, notification operation and feature bit meanings beyond the modern PCI descriptor and narrow helpers.","Console redraw, resize and spawn signaling implementation behind the VT wrappers and fallback stubs.","Serial driver behavior, ioctl handling and RS485 and smartcard programming sequences.","Divisor calculation, baud mapping and interrupt handling flows for UART registers.","DMA setup and device validation callback contract for modern virtio PCI."],"dossier":"D16","findings":[{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/virtio_pci_modern.h::virtio_pci_modern_device"],"text":"Modern PCI transport descriptor bundles a host PCI device reference with mapped control, device, notification and interrupt status windows plus their extent companions, notification mapping and multiplier tuning, bar selection, device identity record, optional device validation hook and DMA addressability limit."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/virtio_pci_modern.h::vp_modern_get_features","include/linux/virtio_pci_modern.h::vp_modern_get_driver_features","include/linux/virtio_pci_modern.h::vp_modern_set_features"],"text":"Feature helpers expose a narrow single-word view over an extended multi-word capability array, converting between representations when sampling device or driver state and when programming accepted features, with driver sampling expecting only the low word to carry bits."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/vt_kern.h::vt_spawn_console"],"text":"Console spawn control aggregates a spinlock with a process handle and a signal number, representing deferred userspace notification state."},{"kind":"lock","sids":["include/linux/vt_kern.h::vt_spawn_console"],"text":"Spawn notification state carries its own spinlock alongside the target process reference and signal value, indicating serialized updates to that small control block."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/vt_kern.h::vt_notifier_param"],"text":"Virtual terminal notification parameter pairs a console instance reference with an unsigned character value describing the update that occurred."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["include/linux/vt.h::vt_kmsg_redirect"],"text":"Kernel message redirection query always reports zero and ignores its argument in this configuration."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["include/linux/vt_kern.h::con_set_trans_old","include/linux/vt_kern.h::con_get_trans_old","include/linux/vt_kern.h::con_set_trans_new","include/linux/vt_kern.h::con_get_trans_new","include/linux/vt_kern.h::con_clear_unimap","include/linux/vt_kern.h::con_set_unimap","include/linux/vt_kern.h::con_get_unimap","include/linux/vt_kern.h::con_set_default_unimap","include/linux/vt_kern.h::con_free_unimap","include/linux/vt_kern.h::con_protect_unimap","include/linux/vt_kern.h::con_copy_unimap"],"text":"In this configuration translation and unicode map management are inert fallbacks where configuration and clearing operations report success without effect, retrieval operations report invalid argument, freeing and protection operations do nothing, and copying between consoles reports success without transfer."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["include/linux/vt_kern.h::update_screen","include/linux/vt_kern.h::switch_screen","include/linux/vt_kern.h::vc_resize"],"text":"Screen refresh aliases delegate to a common redraw routine with a selector distinguishing content update from display switch, while console resizing forwards dimensions to an underlying resize implementation with a fixed boolean flag cleared."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/uapi/linux/serial.h::serial_struct"],"text":"User-visible serial port descriptor records type and line identity, port address and high extension, interrupt, flags, FIFO sizing, divisor and base baud, close timing, I/O method, hub identifier, mapped register base with shift, and an opaque mapping cookie."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/uapi/linux/serial.h::serial_multiport_struct"],"text":"Multiport match descriptor holds a shared interrupt, four port plus mask and match triples, a monitor port and a reserved tail for future expansion."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/uapi/linux/serial.h::serial_icounter_struct"],"text":"Serial event counters tally modem signal transitions, receive and transmit totals, framing and parity and break and overrun conditions, buffer overruns and reserved slots."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/uapi/linux/serial.h::serial_rs485","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::serial_rs485.anon_1","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::serial_rs485.anon_1.anon_1"],"text":"Half-duplex configuration carries feature flags, two RTS timing delays and a trailing variant area that either pads for growth or encodes destination and reception addresses with reserved space."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/uapi/linux/serial.h::SER_RS485_ENABLED","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::SER_RS485_RTS_ON_SEND","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::SER_RS485_RTS_AFTER_SEND","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::SER_RS485_RX_DURING_TX","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::SER_RS485_TERMINATE_BUS","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::SER_RS485_ADDRB","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::SER_RS485_ADDR_RECV","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::SER_RS485_ADDR_DEST","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::SER_RS485_MODE_RS422"],"text":"Half-duplex option bits occupy distinct low positions within a flag word, covering enablement, RTS level during and after transmission, reception during transmission, bus termination, address-mode selection and RS422 mode, with one historical position left unused."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/uapi/linux/serial.h::serial_iso7816"],"text":"Smartcard interface parameters comprise feature flags, guard time, frequency and baud adjustment factors, clock setting and reserved words."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/uapi/linux/serial.h::SER_ISO7816_ENABLED","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::SER_ISO7816_T_PARAM","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::SER_ISO7816_T"],"text":"Smartcard flags reserve the low bit for enablement and a nibble for protocol selection, with a helper that positions a four-bit protocol value into that nibble."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/vt.h::VT_ALLOCATE","include/linux/vt.h::VT_DEALLOCATE","include/linux/vt.h::VT_WRITE","include/linux/vt.h::VT_UPDATE","include/linux/vt.h::VT_PREWRITE"],"text":"Virtual terminal notification codes use consecutive small integers starting at one to distinguish allocation, deallocation, character output, larger updates and pre-write indication."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/uapi/linux/serial.h::ASYNC_CLOSING_WAIT_INF","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::ASYNC_CLOSING_WAIT_NONE"],"text":"Serial close timing sentinels use zero for indefinite wait and the maximum sixteen-bit value for no wait."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/uapi/linux/serial.h::PORT_UNKNOWN","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::PORT_8250","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::PORT_16450","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::PORT_16550","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::PORT_16550A","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::PORT_CIRRUS","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::PORT_16650","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::PORT_16650V2","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::PORT_16750","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::PORT_STARTECH","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::PORT_16C950","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::PORT_16654","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::PORT_16850","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::PORT_RSA","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::PORT_MAX"],"text":"Classic UART type identifiers form a dense zero-based enumeration from unknown through common 8250 family variants up to a defined maximum, allowing user space to name hardware kinds."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/uapi/linux/serial.h::SERIAL_IO_PORT","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::SERIAL_IO_HUB6","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::SERIAL_IO_MEM","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::SERIAL_IO_MEM32","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::SERIAL_IO_AU","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::SERIAL_IO_TSI","include/uapi/linux/serial.h::SERIAL_IO_MEM32BE","include/uapi/linux/serial.